In production, tenant B sees tenant A's orders. What is the bug?

```csharp
public class AppDbContext(DbContextOptions<AppDbContext> o, ITenantContext tenant) : DbContext(o)
{
    protected override void OnModelCreating(ModelBuilder b)
    {
        var tenantId = tenant.TenantId;
        b.Entity<Order>().HasQueryFilter(x => x.TenantId == tenantId);
    }
}
```

A search endpoint builds its filter dynamically. Memory grows steadily, logs show EF compiling a new query on most requests, and `pg_stat_statements` lists thousands of near-identical statements. What is the cause?

```csharp
var p = Expression.Parameter(typeof(Order), "o");
var body = Expression.Equal(
    Expression.Property(p, nameof(Order.CustomerId)),
    Expression.Constant(customerId));
var filter = Expression.Lambda<Func<Order, bool>>(body, p);
var orders = await db.Orders.Where(filter).ToListAsync();
```
